# Admin portal — copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must stay that way.
# In production these are set in the host's secret store, never as a file on disk.
#
# ── The one rule that will bite you ──────────────────────────────────────────
# DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEYS and EMAIL_HMAC_PEPPER must be BYTE-IDENTICAL to the
# public app's. Different keys means the portal cannot read a single contact
# number the site wrote, and cannot match a single address on the allowlist.
#
# Locally you do not copy them at all. Every script in this package — including
# `next dev` and `next build`, which is why they are invoked through `node
# --env-file` rather than the `next` binary directly — loads ../oxvercity/.env
# first and this file second. The public app's .env stays the one source of
# truth and the two cannot drift. Set them below only to override.
#
# In production there is no shared file: each app's host holds its own copy, so
# `npm run admin:verify` checks the two agree by decrypting a row the public
# side wrote. Run it after any key change, before you find out the hard way.

# --- Database ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The portal connects as sxc_admin: full control of the data, append-only on the
# audit log. It refuses to fall back to the owner credential in production.
#
# TLS is demanded in code (src/lib/shared-db.ts), not left to this string, so a
# URL pasted without `sslmode=require` no longer downgrades the connection
# silently. Append it anyway. This link carries every contact number the portal
# decrypts to render a record.
ADMIN_DATABASE_URL=

# --- Public origin -----------------------------------------------------------
# This portal's own origin, used to build invitation links and to check request
# Origin headers. A separate hostname from the public site is the point — a
# cross-site scripting flaw on sxccaa.org cannot reach a cookie set here.
# No trailing slash.
ADMIN_URL=http://localhost:3400

# The public site's origin. Used only to build the links an admin follows out to
# a profile, never to trust anything.
APP_URL=http://localhost:3300

# --- Email (Resend) ----------------------------------------------------------
# INHERITED. Leave these commented out.
#
# Every script here loads ../oxvercity/.env first and this file second, and a
# later --env-file wins — including when its value is EMPTY. So an uncommented
# `RESEND_API_KEY=` here does not mean "unset"; it means "override the working
# key with an empty string", and every invitation silently fails to send.
# Learned the hard way on 11 Sep 2026.
#
# Uncomment only to genuinely override, and then give a real value:
#
#   MAIL_FROM must be on a domain VERIFIED IN RESEND. The public app's domain
#   is the one that is verified; a different local part on it is fine
#   (admin@<verified-domain>), an unverified domain is rejected with a 403.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# MAIL_FROM=SXCCAA Admin <admin@your-verified-domain>
# MAIL_REPLY_TO=admin@your-verified-domain

# --- Secrets (normally inherited from ../oxvercity/.env — see the note above) --
# DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEYS=
# EMAIL_HMAC_PEPPER=
# SESSION_SECRET=
